IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-applications`

-- Tests of sections 60, 61 and 62. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text, as written beside
-- the assertion.

§ `Tests -- sections 60 to 62`

§§ `Section 60(1) to (1.3)`

-- An application and an approval are both needed.
#ASSERT `s 60(1) — a benefit is payable to the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(1) — a benefit is payable to the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(1) — a benefit is payable to the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(1) — a benefit is payable to the person` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Earnings of 2020, a beneficiary of a retirement pension on that day, the Minister has the information: deemed made on 1 January 2021.
#ASSERT `s 60(1.1) — the day an application for a post-retirement benefit is deemed to be made` 2020 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 60(1.1) — the day an application for a post-retirement benefit is deemed to be made` 2020 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 60(1.1) — the day an application for a post-retirement benefit is deemed to be made` 2020 TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 60(1.1) — the day an application for a post-retirement benefit is deemed to be made` 2023 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (YMD 2024 1 1)
-- A contributor born 5 May 1950 is 70 (deemed so from 1 June 2020) on 1 January 2021 and is in receipt of a benefit: the Minister may waive.
#ASSERT `s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 1950 5 5) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- A return of income alone is enough: paragraph (c) says at least one of the two applies.
#ASSERT `s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 1950 5 5) (YMD 2021 1 1) FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 1950 5 5) (YMD 2021 1 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a contributor.
#ASSERT `s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` FALSE (YMD 1950 5 5) (YMD 2021 1 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Born 31 December 1951: 70 on 31 December 2021, deemed so only from 1 January 2022.
#ASSERT `s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 1951 12 31) (YMD 2021 12 31) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 1951 12 31) (YMD 2022 1 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Deemed made and received on the day on which the requirement is waived.
#ASSERT `s 60(1.3) — the day the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been made and received` TRUE (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 60(1.3) — the day the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been made and received` FALSE (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 60(2) to (5)`

-- Died 15 March 2020; the estate applies on 15 March 2021, within 12 months after the death.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- One day later: outside the 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 16) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Before the death: not an application after the death.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2020 3 14) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- A death benefit is excluded.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` `a death benefit` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not made by the estate, a representative, an heir or a prescribed person.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The deceased would not have been entitled.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` `a retirement pension` FALSE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` `a survivor's pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- A post-retirement disability benefit, whenever received.
#ASSERT `s 60(2.1) — an application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved` `a post-retirement disability benefit` (YMD 1990 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- A disability pension, application received after 31 December 1997.
#ASSERT `s 60(2.1) — an application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved` `a disability pension` (YMD 1998 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(2.1) — an application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved` `a disability pension` (YMD 1997 12 31) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(2.1) — an application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved` `a retirement pension` (YMD 2021 1 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Born 10 February 1940, 70 on 10 February 2010, deemed so from 1 March 2010: February 2010 is not after.
#ASSERT `s 60(2.2) — an application referred to in subsection (2) in respect of a retirement pension may be approved for the month` `a retirement pension` (YMD 1940 2 10) (YMD 2010 2 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(2.2) — an application referred to in subsection (2) in respect of a retirement pension may be approved for the month` `a retirement pension` (YMD 1940 2 10) (YMD 2010 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- The restriction is for a retirement pension only.
#ASSERT `s 60(2.2) — an application referred to in subsection (2) in respect of a retirement pension may be approved for the month` `a survivor's pension` (YMD 1940 2 10) (YMD 2000 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- All of (2), (2.1) and (2.2) allow it.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) to (2.2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved for the month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE (YMD 1940 2 10) (YMD 2010 3 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Subsection (2.2): the month is not after age 70.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) to (2.2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved for the month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE (YMD 1940 2 10) (YMD 2010 2 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Subsection (2.1): a disability pension applied for after 1997.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) to (2.2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved for the month` `a disability pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 15) TRUE (YMD 1940 2 10) (YMD 2010 3 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Subsection (2): outside 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 60(2) to (2.2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved for the month` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2020 3 15) (YMD 2021 3 16) (YMD 2021 3 16) TRUE (YMD 1940 2 10) (YMD 2010 3 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- An orphan died 15 June 2015 aged 14; no application; the person having decision-making responsibility applies on 15 June 2016, within one year.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- One day later.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 16) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `a disabled contributor's child's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Not a child's or orphan's benefit.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Died 31 December 1977: not after 1977.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 1977 12 31) (YMD 1970 1 1) TRUE (YMD 1978 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Died 1 January 1978.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 1978 1 1) (YMD 1970 1 1) TRUE (YMD 1978 6 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Aged 19 at the death: had reached 18.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 1996 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- An application had been made at the time of the death.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) FALSE (YMD 2016 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The benefit would not have been payable on an earlier application.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` FALSE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- No person or agency had responsibility at the death: a person the Minister directs may apply.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- No person had responsibility, but the applicant is not one the Minister has directed.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Someone did have responsibility, and it is not the applicant: a direction does not help.
#ASSERT `s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` `an orphan's benefit` TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) (YMD 2000 8 10) TRUE (YMD 2016 6 15) FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(4) — the benefit applied for under subsection (2) or (3) is paid to the payee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(4) — the benefit applied for under subsection (2) or (3) is paid to the payee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(4) — the benefit applied for under subsection (2) or (3) is paid to the payee` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Paragraph (a): the date of the death of the person.
#ASSERT `s 60(5) — the day an application made under subsection (2) or (3) is deemed to have been received` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2015 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2015 6 15)
-- Paragraph (b): the date of the death of the child or orphan, no application having been made before.
#ASSERT `s 60(5) — the day an application made under subsection (2) or (3) is deemed to have been received` FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2015 6 15) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2015 6 15)
#ASSERT `s 60(5) — the day an application made under subsection (2) or (3) is deemed to have been received` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2015 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 60(5) — the day an application made under subsection (2) or (3) is deemed to have been received` FALSE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2015 6 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 60(6) and (7)`

#ASSERT `s 60(6) — an application for a benefit is made as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(6) — an application for a benefit is made as the Act requires` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(6) — an application for a benefit is made as the Act requires` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(6) — an application for a benefit is made as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(7) — the Minister must consider the application at once and notify the applicant in writing of the decision` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(7) — the Minister must consider the application at once and notify the applicant in writing of the decision` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 60(8) to (11.1)`

-- The first month the benefit could have commenced is May 2010, so the month preceding is April 2010; incapacity began in November 2009: the later, April 2010.
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2009 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2010 4 1)
-- Incapacity considered to have commenced in September 2010: the later.
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2010 9 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2010 9 1)
-- Not made on behalf of the person.
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2009 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2009 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Last incapacitated before 1991.
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 1990 12 31) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2009 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An interrupted period that a regulation allows counts.
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2009 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2010 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 5 20) (YMD 2009 11 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The first month is January 2010 and the month preceding it is December 2009; January rolls back across the year end when the first month is January.
#ASSERT `s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (YMD 2010 1 20) (YMD 2009 11 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2009 12 1)
-- Ceased 10 March 2012 after 100 days of incapacity; made on 17 June 2012, the last day of the window. The first month is February 2011, the month preceding January 2011; incapacity began December 2010: January 2011.
#ASSERT `s 60(9) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made by or on behalf of the person after incapacity has ceased to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2012 3 10) 100 (YMD 2012 6 17) (YMD 2011 2 14) (YMD 2010 12 5) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2011 1 1)
-- One day later: outside the window.
#ASSERT `s 60(9) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made by or on behalf of the person after incapacity has ceased to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2012 3 10) 100 (YMD 2012 6 18) (YMD 2011 2 14) (YMD 2010 12 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period of 20 days: made in April 2012, one month after March.
#ASSERT `s 60(9) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made by or on behalf of the person after incapacity has ceased to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2012 3 10) 20 (YMD 2012 4 30) (YMD 2011 2 14) (YMD 2010 12 5) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2011 1 1)
-- Made in May 2012, two months after.
#ASSERT `s 60(9) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made by or on behalf of the person after incapacity has ceased to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE (YMD 2012 3 10) 20 (YMD 2012 5 1) (YMD 2011 2 14) (YMD 2010 12 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The Minister is not satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 60(9) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made by or on behalf of the person after incapacity has ceased to have been made` (YMD 2005 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YMD 2012 3 10) 100 (YMD 2012 6 17) (YMD 2011 2 14) (YMD 2010 12 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 60(10) — the period of incapacity counts` TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(10) — the period of incapacity counts` FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(10) — the period of incapacity counts` FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(11) — subsections (8) to (10) apply to the individual` (YMD 1991 1 1) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(11) — subsections (8) to (10) apply to the individual` (YMD 1990 12 31) EQUALS FALSE
-- A disability pension application deemed made in January 2011, though actually made in June 2012: the child's application may be deemed made in January 2011.
#ASSERT `s 60(11.1) — the month in which the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor's child's benefit to have been made` `a disability pension` (JUST (YMD 2011 1 1)) (YMD 2012 6 5) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2011 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 60(11.1) — the month in which the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor's child's benefit to have been made` `a post-retirement disability benefit` (JUST (YMD 2011 1 1)) (YMD 2012 6 5) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2011 1 1)
-- Deemed made in the same month it was actually made: no earlier month.
#ASSERT `s 60(11.1) — the month in which the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor's child's benefit to have been made` `a disability pension` (JUST (YMD 2012 6 1)) (YMD 2012 6 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not an application for a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit.
#ASSERT `s 60(11.1) — the month in which the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor's child's benefit to have been made` `a retirement pension` (JUST (YMD 2011 1 1)) (YMD 2012 6 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 60(11.1) — the month in which the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor's child's benefit to have been made` `a disability pension` NOTHING (YMD 2012 6 5) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 60(12)`

#ASSERT `s 60(12) — the person must be at the place and time the Minister requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 60(12) — the person must be at the place and time the Minister requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 60(12) — the person must be at the place and time the Minister requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Tests -- section 61`

#ASSERT `s 61(1) — the Minister may approve payment of an interim benefit` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 61(1) — the Minister may approve payment of an interim benefit` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61(1) — the Minister may approve payment of an interim benefit` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 61(1) — the Minister may approve payment of an interim benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- An interim benefit of 800 and an approved benefit of 1000: the beneficiary is paid the additional 200.
#ASSERT `s 61(2)(a) — the additional amount the beneficiary is paid` 800 1000 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 61(2)(a) — the additional amount the beneficiary is paid` 1000 800 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 61(2)(a) — the additional amount the beneficiary is paid` 1000 1000 EQUALS 0
-- An interim benefit of 1000 and an approved benefit of 800: 200 is deducted or recovered.
#ASSERT `s 61(2)(b) — the excess that is deducted from subsequent payments or otherwise recovered` 1000 800 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 61(2)(b) — the excess that is deducted from subsequent payments or otherwise recovered` 800 1000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 61(2)(b) — the excess that is deducted from subsequent payments or otherwise recovered` 1000 1000 EQUALS 0

§ `Tests -- section 62`

#ASSERT `s 62(1) — payment is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment is payable` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 3 18) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — payment is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment is payable` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 1 20) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — payment is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment is payable` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2020 12 20) EQUALS FALSE
-- First payment payable for January 2021 and approved in March 2021: monthly payments from April 2021.
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the month from which monthly payments are made` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 3 18) EQUALS (YMD 2021 4 1)
-- Approved within the month: monthly payments from the first month.
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the month from which monthly payments are made` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 1 20) EQUALS (YMD 2021 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the month from which monthly payments are made` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2020 12 20) EQUALS (YMD 2021 1 1)
-- Approval in December: payments from January of the next year.
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the month from which monthly payments are made` (YMD 2021 11 1) (YMD 2021 12 2) EQUALS (YMD 2022 1 1)
-- January, February and March 2021 are paid in one sum in April.
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the number of months for which payment is made in one sum` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 3 18) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the number of months for which payment is made in one sum` (YMD 2021 1 1) (YMD 2021 1 20) EQUALS 0
-- November and December 2021.
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the number of months for which payment is made in one sum` (YMD 2021 11 1) (YMD 2021 12 2) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `s 62(1) — the number of months for which payment is made in one sum` (YMD 2021 12 1) (YMD 2021 12 20) EQUALS 0
-- Deemed payable at the beginning of the month with which it is payable.
#ASSERT `s 62(2) — the day a benefit is deemed to have become payable` (YMD 2021 4 17) EQUALS (YMD 2021 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 62(2) — the day a benefit is deemed to have become payable` (YMD 2021 4 1) EQUALS (YMD 2021 4 1)
